results=results.replace('Thus the gain is not wholly created by throughput pricing, although its reference magnitude depends substantially on that proxy.', f"At wear prices of 0.01 and 0.04, frozen-signal reoptimization gives {money(-ctrl['wear']['0.01']['frozen_signals_reoptimized']['all299']['micro_mean_difference_aud'])} and {money(-ctrl['wear']['0.04']['frozen_signals_reoptimized']['all299']['micro_mean_difference_aud'])} cents of saving, while matched retraining gives {money(-ctrl['wear']['0.01']['matched_signals_reoptimized']['all299']['micro_mean_difference_aud'])} and {money(-ctrl['wear']['0.04']['matched_signals_reoptimized']['all299']['micro_mean_difference_aud'])} cents. Thus the gain is not wholly created by throughput pricing, although its reference magnitude depends substantially on that proxy.")
results=results.replace('A common 3 kW export protection layer', 'The persistence case supplies a direct private/network counterexample. Under matched retraining, the first and held-out panels save approximately 1.625 and 1.580 cents per owner-day, yet overvoltage exposure increases by 0.373 percentage points (95% interval 0.177 to 0.576) and 0.606 points (0.465 to 0.750); mean daily import peaks increase by about 2.51 kW in both panels. Continuous-state matched retraining instead reduces overexposure by approximately 1.136 and 1.040 points. Private gains under input adaptation therefore do not provide a stable proxy for network value.\n\nA common 3 kW export protection layer')
discussion=discussion.replace('Network outcomes do not reverse that choice consistently.', 'Network outcomes do not reverse that choice consistently. The matched-persistence counterexample is particularly consequential: private saving improves while overvoltage and import peak worsen on both evaluated panels. Network consequences must therefore be rechecked after retraining even when private validation selects a better operating model.')
